\description{
\code{\link[=attribute_lead_lag_duration]{attribute_lead_lag_duration()}} reports the two directional adoption streams
(\code{b_adopts} and \code{a_reverts}) separately, which are neither exhaustive nor
mutually exclusive: an identifier where Source B later adopts Source A's
base-year value \emph{and} Source A later adopts Source B's base-year value is
counted in both streams, while an identifier where both sources later
converge on a new third value (\code{C != A_base} and \code{C != B_base}) is counted
in neither. Moreover, among unresolved disagreements, some identifiers are
observed all the way to the end of the panel without ever agreeing
(uncensored persistent discordance), whereas others drop out of one or both
sources before the end of the panel (right-censored loss to follow-up).
}
\details{
This function partitions all \code{disc_base_n} base-year disagreements into six
strictly mutually exclusive longitudinal trajectories whose counts sum to
\code{disc_base_n} (\verb{100.0\%}).

\strong{The six mutually exclusive trajectories:}
\enumerate{
\item \code{"b_only_adopted_a_base"} -- Source B later adopted Source A's
\code{base_year} value (and Source A did not adopt Source B's \code{base_year}
value).
\item \code{"a_only_adopted_b_base"} -- Source A later adopted Source B's
\code{base_year} value (and Source B did not adopt Source A's \code{base_year}
value).
\item \code{"bidirectional_cross_adoption"} -- Both directional adoptions
occurred in follow-up years (\code{B} adopted \code{A_base} and \code{A} adopted
\code{B_base}).
\item \code{"converged_new_third_value"} -- Neither source adopted the other's
\code{base_year} value, but both sources reported the \emph{same} new value
(\code{A_t == B_t}) in at least one follow-up year \code{t > base_year}.
\item \code{"unresolved_uncensored_persistent"} -- Never converged through any
of trajectories 1--4, and both sources observed the identifier in
\code{max_panel_year}.
\item \code{"unresolved_right_censored"} -- Never converged through any of
trajectories 1--4, and one or both sources lacked an observation for the
identifier in \code{max_panel_year} (administrative or attrition censoring).
}
